# Windows Log Collection Pipeline

## Overview

This document explains how security telemetry is generated, collected, forwarded, indexed, and analyzed within the SOC Home Lab.

---

## Architecture

Windows Activity

↓

Windows Event Logs

↓

Sysmon

↓

Windows Event Log Channels

↓

Splunk Universal Forwarder

↓

TCP 9997

↓

Splunk Enterprise

↓

Indexed Events

↓

Searches, Dashboards and Detections

---

## Data Sources

- Security
- System
- Application
- Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational

---

## Universal Forwarder

The Universal Forwarder continuously monitors configured Windows Event Log channels using `inputs.conf`.

Collected events are securely forwarded to Splunk Enterprise over TCP port 9997.

---

## Splunk Enterprise

Splunk Enterprise receives endpoint telemetry, indexes incoming events, and provides centralized searching, monitoring, and detection capabilities.

